<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31395" root="غبق" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَبْقَانُ</span></b> , applied to a man, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَبْقَى</span> [for which
the CK has <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَبْقَآءُ</span>], applied to a woman, (O, K,
TA,) epithets similar to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَبْحَانُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَبْحَى</span>, (O,)
irregularly formed, for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعْلَانُ</span> is not to be formed
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِفْتَعَلَ</span> nor from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَعَّلَ</span>, (TA,) <i>Who has drunk
an evening-draught,</i> or <i>what is termed a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيُوق</span>. (K.)

